    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7b8828c1e8d6c33a4a36fa57ec99c49771c9ac62ba5158e04d376f67df7303fc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The first unit obtains vague convergence of the measures m_y from Mertens' summatory totient estimate, passing from interval indicators to compactly supported test functions by Abel summation, and identifies that limit with periodic-horocycle equidistribution. The second unit retains the same measure family but changes representation: logarithmic transport exposes Euler-weighted discrete points and the Farey connection, while the Mellin transform converts dilation into a product separating the test-function transform from zeta-controlled arithmetic singularities. Arithmetic counting, dynamics, and Mellin analysis are therefore linked through one measure family and a concrete sequence of representation changes.",
